The interaction that produces the rent, with the measured cause columns. The revision gain is crossed with the number of balancing rounds in the noise-only environment of Section 6.2, sixteen seeds per cell. Neither factor alone moves output: with the balancing rounds at zero a gain of one leaves output at its no-revision level, and with the gain at zero three rounds of balancing do the same. The loss appears only in the combination and grows in both directions, to 0.8738 at a gain of one with three rounds. The mechanism is labour feasibility, and the cause columns say so: the plan step lowers at least one target in 0 to 66 of 80 quarters as the gain rises, investment falls from 0.0500 to 0.0434 of base, the capital stock ends at 0.903 of base, labour utilisation falls from 0.870 to 0.710 and spoilage rises from 0.1 to 2.9 per cent of supply. The inventory channel is absent: making the inventory estimate noiseless, removing it, or setting the stock ratio to zero or one half leaves the loss unchanged, and at base-year targets the feasibility programme returns the target unchanged even at half the base inventory.
